= Reformist leaders resign

Our policy choices have greatly offended the reformist faction. Many of our most experienced leaders have resigned.

Many reformists have joined a new party, the *Sozial-Republikanische Partei Deutschlands* (Social-Republican Party of Germany), founded by former Reichsbanner leader Otto Hörsing. They proclaim their desire to defend the Republic, and see us as having strayed from a pure Republican path. The new party claims some worker and middle-class support.
